P0 CRYPTO REVIEW

The current push is still hand-implementing security standards we
explicitly decided not to rebuild.

A. src/qp/obsigna/canonical.ts is NOT a correct RFC 8785 implementation.

Examples of incorrect behavior in current code:
- serializes undefined as the literal string "undefined"
- serializes NaN as "NaN"
- serializes Infinity/-Infinity
- custom number formatting instead of required ECMAScript JSON number
serialization
- custom string handling and sorting rather than a verified JCS implementat=
ion

RFC 8785 requires I-JSON-compatible input and Appendix G explicitly
lists the JavaScript npm package canonicalize as a verified compatible
implementation:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8785.html
Reference implementation:
https://github.com/cyberphone/json-canonicalization
JS package:
https://www.npmjs.com/package/canonicalize

FIX:
- delete custom canonicalizer from production path
- install pinned canonicalize version only if upstream Obsigna does
not already expose the needed canonicalization/hash API
- invalid JCS inputs (NaN/Infinity/undefined/lone invalid values) MUST
fail; never invent serialized tokens
- import upstream RFC vectors and test byte-for-byte
- cross-check same fixture in JS + Obsigna Python/Go vector outputs.

B. Stop writing =E2=80=9CObsigna-compatible=E2=80=9D. Actually use Obsigna.

Upstream:
https://github.com/agent-receipts/obsigna
Current repository snapshot inspected: main around
5c3d41c1bbdcda298f52f7608b8c589999694e43
Current TS package inspected:
  @obsigna/sdk-ts 0.17.0
  Node >=3D22.11.0
  Apache-2.0

Upstream already implements:
- RFC 8785 canonicalization
- Ed25519 signing
- receipt hash
- chain verification
- chain_id and sequence checks
- terminal semantics
- key rotation
- raw on-wire verification
- response-hash verification
- cross-language vectors
- MUST-reject conformance corpus
- KMS/HSM Signer abstraction

DELETE/DEMOTE:
- src/qp/receipts.ts custom signer/envelope
- src/qp/obsigna/canonical.ts
- custom receipt chain/hash/signature functions wherever equivalent
upstream functions exist

KEEP OUR CODE ONLY FOR:
- constructing the QP extension payload
- validating extension schema
- QP semantic replay
- mapping private evidence/disclosure roots into signed receipt fields

Use upstream signReceipt/hashReceipt/verifyReceipt/verifyChain APIs.
For verification, trust key comes from configured trust policy /
pinned operator-log key, NEVER from a key carried by the receipt
itself.

Run Obsigna=E2=80=99s upstream conformance/must-reject vectors in CI.
Important test:
1. valid Agent Receipt + QP extension =3D> crypto PASS
2. mutate any signed extension field =3D> crypto FAIL
3. validly signed receipt containing insufficient/false evidence =3D>
crypto PASS, QP semantic FAIL
This preserves SIGNED !=3D TRUE.

C. Receipt extension must be signed, not side-loaded.
Replay V2 currently accepts a separately supplied ReplayInput. That
creates a substitution surface.
The signed receipt itself must contain:
  qp.contract_root
  qp.claim_id
  qp.spec_id
  qp.spec_version
  qp.actuality
  qp.evidence_root
  qp.judge_results_root
  qp.gate_results_root
  qp.state_before_root
  qp.state_after_root
  qp.authority_root/ref
  qp.privacy/disclosure_root
  qp.attestation_root if applicable
Semantic replay parses exactly those signed fields from the receipt.
Caller cannot provide an alternate qpExtension object.

D. Upgrade module/runtime coherently.
Current pmail package says CommonJS while tsconfig is ESNext/Bundler.
Obsigna TS package is ESM.
Move pmail deliberately to:
- Node 22.12+ pinned in CI/runtime
- "type": "module"
- explicit exports/build config
- no accidental CJS/ESM dual behavior

E. Signer architecture.
MVP:
- dev signer only in tests
Production:
- signer key outside normal agent/planner process
- use Obsigna Signer abstraction backed by HSM/KMS or dstack-derived
key when TEE mode is enabled
- key id/trust policy pinned externally
- key rotation represented using upstream protocol, not ad-hoc key replacem=
ent

Do not merge any new custom cryptographic serializer, receipt format,
signature wrapper or chain format without proving upstream cannot
represent the requirement.

Acceptance:
- @obsigna/sdk-ts pinned
- upstream conformance passes
- no homegrown JCS in prod path
- no receipt self-authentication
- mutation of qp extension breaks signature
- a signed lie still fails QP semantic replay.
